.TH WEACT-LIST 1 "October 2026" "WeAct35 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
weact-list \- list WeAct USB displays without opening serial ports
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B weact-list
.RB [ --verbose | --help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
weact-list reads Linux sysfs tty metadata and existing /dev/serial/by-id links.
It does not open a serial node and sends no display commands.  For VID:PID
1a86:fe0c, Product Display FS V1 is reported as FS35 and Display FS 0.96 Inch
as FS096; another Product is reported as UNKNOWN.  Serial and manufacturer can
be unavailable.  Devices are listed in tty-name order.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --verbose
Include sysfs, USB interface, driver and interface identifiers.
.TP
.B --help
Print usage.
.SH OUTPUT
Output identifies tty, model, USB Product and available stable by-id path.
Use the by-id path for later hardware commands.  Inventory is not permission
to write and does not prove that a display is available for a guarded command.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
weact-list
weact-list --verbose
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 means a completed scan, including no devices; 1 means incomplete scan or
output error; 2 means invalid arguments.  Missing optional fields print as a
dash.  Stale/disconnected links are skipped, with detail in verbose mode.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR weact-cli (1),
.BR weactterm (1)
